# strelka_material is compiled by three compilers: NVCC, the Metal compiler, and
# the host C++ compiler for the doctest suite. clang-tidy only ever sees the
# third, so a suggestion that reaches for the C++ standard library -- <numbers>,
# <ranges>, std::cmp_less -- would fix the host build and break the two device
# builds no analyzer here runs over.
#
# Correctness, UB and performance checks still apply: those are about what the
# code does, and it does the same thing under all three.
#
# Scope, exactly: clang-tidy picks its config from the *translation unit*, not
# from the header a diagnostic lands in, and this directory is an INTERFACE
# target with no TU of its own. So this file governs editor integration -- which
# is the only way tidy runs in this repo, see CLAUDE.md -- and not a batch
# run-clang-tidy over compile_commands.json, where these headers are reached
# through tests/material/*.cpp and answer to the root config instead.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -modernize-*
